id: pm-2lex4r
title: "pm measure: a named population over the workspace declared as data, with a composable source vocabulary and derived arithmetic so a bound can be denominated in the unit it actually means"
description: "A measurement is a named, saved, declarative query over the workspace that resolves to a number or a labelled set of numbers. Sources compose: items (a filter expression over status/type/tags/priority/fields/dates), dependency_kind (typed edge counts), graph (any numeric field of any analytic — analyze, redundancy, articulation, centrality, communities, dominators, slack), validate and health (warning and check populations), history (counts over the immutable stream: ops, authors, provenance fields, inter-arrival recurrence), links (linked file/test/doc presence and staleness), and provider (contributed by an extension). The decisive addition is derived: an arithmetic expression over other measurements, evaluated by the SDK. Denomination is the difference between a bound that can be satisfied by a repair and one that cannot. A floor over total graph edges forbids removing a transitively implied edge, because the total falls; a floor over total-minus-redundant is neutral to that exact repair and still breaches on the removal of a load-bearing edge. Today that distinction requires editing a number by hand, which makes a cleanup byte-indistinguishable from an erosion in the resulting diff. With derived measurements the unit carries the intent, so the enforcement mechanism can tell the two apart without a privileged act. Measurements are addressable by id from every read surface, so an agent composes them with grep and jq, and every measurement reports the cost it incurred to compute."
type: Feature
status: open
priority: 1
tags[5]: "area:sdk",assurance,configurability,measurement,query
created_at: "2026-08-10T20:55:41.413Z"
updated_at: "2026-08-10T20:55:41.413Z"
author: "harness:claude-code"
estimated_minutes: 600
acceptance_criteria: "A measurement is created, listed, read, updated and removed through pm commands, persisted as workspace data, and recorded in the immutable history like any other mutation; The source vocabulary covers items, dependency_kind, graph analytics, validate, health, history, links, and extension-contributed providers, and each source declares its own key schema so a declaration naming a removed field fails loudly instead of reading as zero; derived measurements evaluate arithmetic over other measurements, with cycle detection, so denomination is expressible without code; Every evaluation reports its own compute cost and honours an explicit bound on it, so a measurement remains affordable at a million items; Measurement results are addressable in json and toon and stable enough to pipe into jq, with the selector documented in the row contract"
